# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ActivityPub implementations funded by NLnet.
#
# Source: https://nlnet.nl/project/ — the "All projects" table filtered with the
# page's own ActivityPub keyword search (retrieved 2026-11-04), one record per
# distinct codebase. The funded projects themselves, with their NLnet page as
# id, are in data/nlnet.ttl (ex:Funding); this section only holds the software.
#
# doap:implements names https://www.w3.org/TR/activitypub/, the W3C
# Recommendation already in the catalog (data/dump/w3c/specs.nq), so the UI
# joins these records to the specification without a second local copy.
#
# The 60 grants in data/nlnet.ttl map to the 45 codebases below: several
# projects were funded more than once, and each ex:Funding keeps its own grant
# period.
#
# Homepages and repositories come from the NLnet project pages. Where a page
# links only a forge organisation, that URL is kept as the source-code location
# (and gets no doap:GitRepository type below). Where a page lists no source at
# all, the project's own repository is used, and three records have no link yet
# (their comments say so). Licenses are omitted: the NLnet pages do not state
# one. doap:maintainer is likewise omitted — the grants name projects, not the
# people in data/identities.json.
#
# doap:implements records the specification the funded work targets. That is
# the server protocol for implementations and libraries, and the protocol they
# interoperate with for the client apps (Tusky, PixelDroid, ActivityPub PWA).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ActivityBot — NLnet: ActivityBot.
